<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Cornish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1715–1770</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Samuel Cornish was a British admiral. In 1762, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>, he commanded the naval force from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> that carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-draper">William Draper</a>'s troops to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> and helped capture the city from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He was made a baronet in 1766.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-cornish.jpg" alt="Samuel Cornish" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Kearney · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samuel_Cornish_in_1825_by_Francis_Kearney.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
